# Godot 4+ specific ignores
.godot/
.import/
# Godot 4 keeps per-asset import metadata next to the asset as
# <asset>.import, where Godot 3 kept it all under .import/ (the line
# above). Both are generated on first import and regenerate from the
# asset itself, so neither is tracked here.
#
# Note this is the opposite of Godot's own recommendation, which is to
# commit *.import so the uid:// each one carries stays stable across
# machines. That matters when scenes reference assets by UID; everything
# in this project references them by res:// path instead, so the only
# effect of tracking them would be 89 generated files churning their
# UIDs whenever someone reimports. Flip this if that ever changes.
*.import
export.cfg
export_presets.cfg

# Imported translations (automatically generated from CSV files)
*.translation

# Mono-specific ignores
.mono/
data_*/

# Personal Claude Code settings (not shared)
.claude/settings.local.json

# Згенерований зведений файл реплік — джерело правди лишається в data/visitors/*.tres
# (tools/DialogueIO.tscn, DIALOGUE_MODE=export)
dialogue.md
